From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 03:25:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: HDMI 3D frame packing on a dual-mode DisplayPort
 connector too

nvidia-drm offered HDMI 3D frame packing on HDMI connectors only: those
set stereo_allowed, and the atomic check refused a frame packed mode on
any other connector. A dual-mode DisplayPort connector (a DP++ port of
the card with a passive HDMI adaptor, or the HDMI port of a laptop wired
to such a port through a level shifter) has a TMDS output of the GPU,
which NVKMS drives as HDMI, with its InfoFrames: nvidia-drm gives that
connector the HDMI properties and NV_DUAL_MODE_TMDS (the patch before).
NVKMS validates frame packing for a display it drives through a TMDS
output, never through a DisplayPort protocol (nvDpyEvoSupportsHdmi3D()),
and within the pixel clock of a passive DisplayPort adaptor, which it
asks the resource manager for (nvDpyProbeMaxPixelClock(): 165 MHz for a
DVI adaptor or what an HDMI adaptor of type 1 or 2 says). So a frame
packed mode that it lists on such a connector is one the TMDS output and
the adaptor carry, with NVKMS's 3D vendor InfoFrame; it was refused all
the same.

A dual-mode connector now sets stereo_allowed when it gets its TMDS
output, and takes a frame packed mode under the same condition as an
HDMI connector (nv_drm_connector_takes_frame_packing()): its display
advertised frame packing, as NVKMS validated it, when its modes were last
probed. On the DisplayPort output NVKMS validates no frame packing, so
the list of modes and what is taken are what they were; an HDMI
connector is as before.

Checked on the host, with the function as the header has it: 10 checks,
and three mutants of the decision each fail; nvidia-drm.ko of driver 620
and of driver 580 built against Linux 7.3.4 without a warning in it.

Not tried with a 3D display on hardware.
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c |  9 +++++++++
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.h | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c      |  9 +++++++--
 3 files changed, 36 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c
index b17adb7..a555e93 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c
@@ -1938,6 +1938,15 @@ void nv_drm_connector_add_dual_mode_tmds(struct nv_drm_connector *nv_connector)
 
     nv_connector->dual_mode_tmds = true;
 
+    /*
+     * Hades: HDMI 3D frame packing too, as on an HDMI connector: the probe
+     * helper keeps the frame packed modes that nv_drm_connector_get_modes()
+     * lists, which NVKMS validates only for the TMDS output
+     * (nv_drm_connector_takes_frame_packing()). A display on the DisplayPort
+     * output gets no mode with a 3D layout, and its list is what it was.
+     */
+    nv_connector->base.stereo_allowed = true;
+
     NV_DRM_DEV_LOG_INFO(
         nv_dev,
         "Connector at physical index %u is a dual-mode DisplayPort connector: its TMDS output is offered as HDMI",
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.h b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.h
index 3b08d36..d4fd9de 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.h
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.h
@@ -141,6 +141,26 @@ static inline NvU64 nv_drm_dual_mode_tmds_value(bool connected,
     return (connected && tmds_encoder) ? 1 : 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Hades: a connector takes an HDMI 3D frame packed mode: an HDMI connector, or
+ * a dual-mode DisplayPort one (nv_drm_connector_add_dual_mode_tmds()), whose
+ * display advertised frame packing, as NVKMS validated it, when its modes were
+ * last probed (frame_packing_advertised). NVKMS validates frame packing only
+ * for a display that it drives through a TMDS output, never through a
+ * DisplayPort protocol (nvDpyEvoSupportsHdmi3D()), and within the pixel clock
+ * of a passive DisplayPort adaptor (nvDpyProbeMaxPixelClock()): on a dual-mode
+ * connector the frame packed modes come only from its TMDS output, where the
+ * GPU sends HDMI itself, through the level shifter of the port or a passive
+ * adaptor, with the 3D vendor InfoFrame of NVKMS, as on an HDMI connector.
+ */
+static inline bool nv_drm_connector_takes_frame_packing(
+    bool hdmi_connector,
+    bool dual_mode_tmds,
+    bool frame_packing_advertised)
+{
+    return (hdmi_connector || dual_mode_tmds) && frame_packing_advertised;
+}
+
 void nv_drm_connector_add_dual_mode_tmds(struct nv_drm_connector *nv_connector);
 void nv_drm_connector_add_hdr10plus(struct nv_drm_connector *nv_connector,
                                     NvU32 routes);
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
index 2d6418c..b2dd046 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
@@ -2803,6 +2803,8 @@ static int head_modeset_config_attach_connector(
  * Check what an HDMI 3D frame packed mode needs from the connectors of its
  * crtc: an HDMI connector, whose display advertised frame packing when its
  * modes were last probed, and no user-provided vendor specific infoframe.
+ * (Hades: or a dual-mode DisplayPort connector, by its TMDS output:
+ * nv_drm_connector_takes_frame_packing().)
  *
  * NVKMS tells the display that the picture is frame packed with its own HDMI
  * vendor specific infoframe, and the NV_HDMI_VSIF_METADATA property replaces
@@ -2836,8 +2838,11 @@ static int nv_drm_crtc_atomic_check_frame_packed(
             continue;
         }
 
-        if ((nv_connector->type != NVKMS_CONNECTOR_TYPE_HDMI) ||
-            !nv_connector->frame_packing_advertised) {
+        /* Hades: or a dual-mode DisplayPort connector, by its TMDS output */
+        if (!nv_drm_connector_takes_frame_packing(
+                nv_connector->type == NVKMS_CONNECTOR_TYPE_HDMI,
+                nv_connector->dual_mode_tmds,
+                nv_connector->frame_packing_advertised)) {
             NV_DRM_DEV_DEBUG_DRIVER(
                 nv_dev,
                 "The display does not advertise HDMI 3D frame packing");
-- 
2.53.0

